-- title:
--   Source algebra $C^*(I_A,a)$, marked words and degree spaces $\mathcal F^A_t$
-- statement:
--   Let $a_1,\dots,a_s$ be complex $N_A\times N_A$ matrices, the **marked generators**, and let $\mathcal A=C^*(I_A,a_1,\dots,a_s)$ be the unital $*$-subalgebra of matrices they generate.
--
--   1. A **marked word** of length $\ell$ is an ordered product $a_{i_1}^{\epsilon_1}\cdots a_{i_\ell}^{\epsilon_\ell}$ of $\ell$ generators or their adjoints, $\epsilon_j\in\{1,*\}$; the empty word is the identity $I_A$ and has length zero.
--   2. The **degree-at-most-$t$ space** is
--
--   $$\mathcal F^A_t=\operatorname{span}\{I_A,\ a_{i_1}^{\epsilon_1}\cdots a_{i_\ell}^{\epsilon_\ell}:\ \ell\le t,\ \epsilon_j\in\{1,*\}\},$$
--
--   a complex subspace of $\mathcal A$ (eq. (43)).
--
--   Every noncommutative $*$-polynomial of degree at most $t$ in the generators lies in $\mathcal F^A_t$; these spaces are the filtration on which the relative distance and the degree–distance criterion are stated. The target spaces are $\mathcal F^B_t=\pi(\mathcal F^A_t)$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mathcal A$ is `StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range a)`; in finite dimension the generated $*$-subalgebra is already norm closed, hence equal to the generated C$^*$-algebra (App. E, p.85). A word is a list of pairs $(i,\epsilon)$ with the Boolean `true` meaning the adjoint letter; `wordEval` multiplies the letters in order, and the empty list gives $I_A$.
-- source:
--   Shang, Stilck França, From Simple Sources to Quantum Advantage: Homomorphic Polynomial Transduction via Relative Decoding, arXiv:2609.35101 (held version, sha256 d2be7859…), §4.1, p.17 (A = C∗(I_A, a)), p.18 (marked words, eq. (43)) (pdf_pages 17–18); App. E, p.85

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace RelDecoding

/-- The **source algebra** `A = C∗(I_A, a₁, …, a_s) ⊆ B(H_A)`: the unital ∗-subalgebra of
`Matrix nA nA ℂ` generated by the marked generators `a₁, …, a_s`. Shang, Stilck França,
arXiv:2609.35101 (held version, sha256 d2be7859…), §4.1, p.17.

**Formalization Note.** In finite dimension the ∗-subalgebra generated by the `aᵢ` is already
norm closed, so it is the C∗-algebra they generate (App. E, proof of Lemma E.1, p.85). The
generators carry no assumption (not self-adjoint, not unitary). -/
abbrev genAlg {nA : Type*} [Fintype nA] [DecidableEq nA] {s : ℕ}
    (a : Fin s → Matrix nA nA ℂ) : StarSubalgebra ℂ (Matrix nA nA ℂ) :=
  StarAlgebra.adjoin ℂ (Set.range a)

/-- The marked generator `aᵢ` as an element of `A = C∗(I_A, a)`. -/
def gen {nA : Type*} [Fintype nA] [DecidableEq nA] {s : ℕ}
    (a : Fin s → Matrix nA nA ℂ) (i : Fin s) : genAlg a :=
  ⟨a i, StarAlgebra.subset_adjoin ℂ _ (Set.mem_range_self i)⟩

/-- The value of one letter `(i, ϵ)` of a marked word: `aᵢ` if `ϵ = false` (exponent `1`), and
`aᵢ∗` if `ϵ = true` (exponent `∗`). -/
def letterEval {nA : Type*} [Fintype nA] [DecidableEq nA] {s : ℕ}
    (a : Fin s → Matrix nA nA ℂ) (l : Fin s × Bool) : genAlg a :=
  if l.2 then star (gen a l.1) else gen a l.1

/-- The value `a_{i₁}^{ϵ₁} ⋯ a_{i_ℓ}^{ϵ_ℓ}` in `A` of a **marked word**, a list of letters
`(i, ϵ)` with `ϵ = true` meaning the adjoint. Shang, Stilck França, arXiv:2609.35101 (held
version, sha256 d2be7859…), §4.1, p.18: "A marked word of length ℓ is an ordered product of ℓ
marked generators or their adjoints. The empty word is the identity and has length zero; each
generator or adjoint counts as one letter."

**Formalization Note.** The length of the word is the length of the list; the empty list
evaluates to the identity `I_A`. -/
def wordEval {nA : Type*} [Fintype nA] [DecidableEq nA] {s : ℕ}
    (a : Fin s → Matrix nA nA ℂ) (w : List (Fin s × Bool)) : genAlg a :=
  (w.map (letterEval a)).prod

/-- The **degree-at-most-`t` space** `𝓕ᴬ_t = span{I_A, a_{i₁}^{ϵ₁} ⋯ a_{i_ℓ}^{ϵ_ℓ} : ℓ ≤ t,
ϵⱼ ∈ {1, ∗}}`, a complex subspace of `A`. Shang, Stilck França, arXiv:2609.35101 (held version,
sha256 d2be7859…), §4.1, eq. (43), p.18.

**Formalization Note.** `I_A` is the value of the empty word (length `0 ≤ t`), so it is in the
spanning set. The target spaces `𝓕ᴮ_t = π(𝓕ᴬ_t)` of (43) are the images
`(markedSpace a t).map π.toLinearMap` and are not given a separate name. -/
def markedSpace {nA : Type*} [Fintype nA] [DecidableEq nA] {s : ℕ}
    (a : Fin s → Matrix nA nA ℂ) (t : ℕ) : Submodule ℂ (genAlg a) :=
  Submodule.span ℂ {x | ∃ w : List (Fin s × Bool), w.length ≤ t ∧ wordEval a w = x}

end RelDecoding


